/*
 * image_type.h
 *
 * What kind of file the image holds. The type decides what the platform does with the file, so choose it carefully.  **Firmware (whole operating-system images):** - &#x60;fw&#x60;: a complete firmware bundle for creating devices, such as an iOS IPSW or a Corellium &#x60;.coreimg&#x60; package. Install it cluster-wide with &#x60;installFirmware&#x60;, or upload it at domain level (no &#x60;projectId&#x60; or &#x60;instanceId&#x60;) so device creation can find it. - &#x60;fwpackage&#x60;: another name for &#x60;fw&#x60;. It is stored as &#x60;fw&#x60;, and v3 responses report &#x60;fw&#x60; images as &#x60;fwpackage&#x60;. - &#x60;iotfirmware&#x60;: firmware for IoT and embedded device models, such as an ELF executable, a raw binary, or a ZIP with a &#x60;LOAD.TXT&#x60; load map. - &#x60;fwbinary&#x60;: another name for &#x60;iotfirmware&#x60;. v3 responses report &#x60;iotfirmware&#x60; images as &#x60;fwbinary&#x60;. - &#x60;fwasset&#x60;: a JSON file of firmware assets (for example decryption keys), not firmware itself. Install it with &#x60;installFirmwareAssets&#x60;. - &#x60;clbi&#x60;: a Cellebrite firmware image. Like &#x60;fw&#x60;, a Cellebrite firmware image uploaded at domain level (no &#x60;projectId&#x60; or &#x60;instanceId&#x60;) is offered as a choice when you create a device.  **Files for a specific device:** - &#x60;partition&#x60;: replacement contents for one storage partition of a device. The platform needs a device model to check it against: attach it to a device with &#x60;instanceId&#x60;, or pass &#x60;flavor&#x60; on the image-upload routes. &#x60;name&#x60; must be a partition that model lets users upload. - Other types such as &#x60;kernel&#x60;, &#x60;devicetree&#x60;, &#x60;ramdisk&#x60;, &#x60;media&#x60; and &#x60;extension&#x60; name the kind of file; the endpoint that uses each one describes it.  **MATRIX files** (always attached to an instance, and never replaced by later uploads): - &#x60;mast-wordlist&#x60;: a text file of sensitive values for a MATRIX assessment to search for. - &#x60;mast-frida&#x60;: a Frida script to load during a MATRIX assessment. - &#x60;mast-report&#x60;: a report generated by MATRIX. Created by the platform, not uploaded.  Some types require a license feature. Using one your license does not include fails with 403.
 */

